d author badges such as PRO or BUSINESS next to creator names. At the bottom is a Categories section showcasing rounded square tiles representing video genres including Ads and Commercials, Animation, Branded Content, Comedy, Documentary, Experimental, in a horizontal scroll arrangement with partial tiles visible on the right. The color palette is mostly neutral with white backgrounds, light grays, black text, and subtle blue highlights for active states and clickable links. Typography uses a clean, modern sans-serif font consistent with professional digital platforms, likely around 14-16px base size for text with varying weights for headings and labels. UI elements include icons on buttons, thumbnails with overlay timecodes, buttons with hover states, text links, and a search bar at the top with a search icon placeholder. The layout uses consistent grid alignment and spacing with about 24-32px padding around sections and card margins about 16px. The screen exhibits a minimalist and clean style that focuses on content discoverability and efficient media management. There are no visible animations.\n- **Layout**: The screen layout is divided into two main vertical sections: a fixed narrow left sidebar navigation column, and a wide right main content area. The sidebar features a vertical stacked list of navigation items with 7 menu elements and additional info at the bottom. The main content column is vertically segmented into four horizontal groups stacked top to bottom: (1) an action button bar with 5 equally spaced rectangular buttons; (2) a 'Recent videos' horizontal card row with a placeholder for new video plus 3 video cards; (3) a 'My feed' horizontal scrollable card strip showing multiple video cards arranged in a row with partial cards visible on edges; (4) a 'Categories' horizontal scroll area with rectangular category tiles arranged side by side with partial tiles visible on the right. The right side uses a grid-like arrangement per section with consistent horizontal gutters and vertical spacing. Cards and tiles align uniformly with generous padding around content, and section headings have 'View all' links aligned to the right side horizontally. The overall layout uses a fixed sidebar and a flexible main content area with horizontal scrolling in feed and categories sections for better content access.\n- **Functions**: Users can perform multiple tasks on this interface: at the smallest level, they can enter search queries in the search bar to find videos, folders, or other content; they can click on buttons to upload media locally, import from cloud drives, record video, create templates, or start webinars, each supported by clear icons and text for easy recognition; users can also interact with video thumbnails by clicking on them to view or manage videos, use action icons to share or move videos, and monitor video details such as title, duration, and timestamps. Medium-level tasks consist of browsing recently uploaded or managed videos under 'Recent videos,' keeping track of personalized recommended content under 'My feed' with videos added to staff picks, and exploring content sorted by Categories to discover new videos. Larger workflows include managing the video library by uploading and organizing videos, engaging with recommended or staff-picked content, and categorizing videos by genre or type. The broader goal of this screen is to provide users with an intuitive hub for video content management, discovery, and creation on a digital video platform. It ensures clarity and efficiency through clean layout, clear categorization, and distinct actions, facilitating user workflows around uploading, organizing, discovering, and starting live or recorded video sessions.\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 114\n- **Name**: Vimeo\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/114\n- **Domain**: vimeo.com\n- **Categories**: Social Networking, Entertainment, Video Streaming\n- **Description**: The world's only all-in-one video solutio